WEBVTT

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:16.960
No two ways about it.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:17.920
This is the place.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.040
Here's point zero.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.630
This is where the Yufang sprung up from.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:23.660
And where they disappeared to once again.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:26.210
It's been a whole 70 years now.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.630
But there's got to be some sort
of clue somewhere around here.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:55.250
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:59.740
Flying through the mesh of clouds

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.330
Our dancing wings wrap up in the wind

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:06.750
Stars fall right before our eyes

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:16.050
The blue of all blues that drew us in

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:19.350
We kicked up off the blurring ground

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:24.330
Let me hear the sound of the sky you know

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:33.650
Take flight make gravity your ally

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:40.040
One more time, however many 
times, laughing all along

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:47.130
We would never look back when we fly

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:52.400
An everlasting dream we 
live in pursuit of tomorrow

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.830
Amid rising despair I locked away my love

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:58.130
I hate my weak self

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:04.080
Here and now passes by as 
we head towards the future

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:20.290
Blood for a Nazarin Pound

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:19.170
Is it just me or does Kate look 
like she's lagging behind?

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:20.290
She sure does.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:28.210
Whatcha gonna do now?

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:41.630
There it is! That Kate special!

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:45.000
It's hard to keep your wits 
about you when she pulls that.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.810
Yeah, well, she can only pull that off 'cause that
carburetor can still pump

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.140
through the negative g-force.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:50.330
You stinkin' little...!

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:53.500
And bam, you're dead! Kylie down!

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:54.500
Shut up, you twerp!

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.030
Dead as dead can be!

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:59.890
Natsuo, Kate's the one loaded 
up with cheap fuel, right?

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:02.460
Yep. There was a great 
ol' sale the other day.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:06.830
But lemme tell you, I don't care how cheap it is,
if it don't burn it ain't worth piss.

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:09.830
So I thought we best put 
it to the test first.

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.040
How cheap is cheap?

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.500
About half the price of what we always use.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.170
What a fine deal!

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:17.790
You sure that's really even gasoline?

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:20.040
That's easy enough to tell 
when you get your hands on it.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:22.630
What is it you're testing, then?

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:23.580
The octane rating.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.540
That's the cutest name I ever heard!

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:26.830
Awk Tane! Ock Tain!

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:28.250
What's "ock-tane?"

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:32.290
The higher the octane rating,
the lower the likelihood of autoignition.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:37.290
Which is why high power engines
require high octane gasoline.

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:40.290
Can you determine as much just by flying?

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:43.000
You can tell as soon as you take off,
but there's no knowing until you do.

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:44.960
Kylie.

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:45.960
How was it?

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.750
I hate fighting Kate.

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:50.420
I'd say I did pretty good 
out there today, though!

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:51.540
How 'bout you, Kate?

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:52.960
I noticed multiple cases of knocking.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.630
I estimate at least a three 
percent drop in performance.

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:56.920
Was there an issue with maintenance?

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.710
I'm sure glad I had you handle this for me.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:00.750
What's that supposed to mean?

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.630
Kate was flying up there with 
a tank full of cheap gas.

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:05.170
What?! I didn't know that!

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:06.510
Because I didn't tell you.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:09.550
But now we know why it was so cheap.

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:12.040
Maybe we'd best just drop it all together.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:14.170
Who on earth was even selling it that cheap?

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:16.130
The Standon Oil Company, out in Ikesuka.

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:17.580
They're one of the biggest companies around.

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:19.670
Where do you usually buy from?

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:20.500
From out in Nanko.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:24.740
So you mean, Kate wasn't flying with
the same horsepower she usually has?

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:26.610
So you didn't do "pretty 
good out there" today,

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:28.900
it was just that Kate was being held back!

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:32.500
Gah! And here I was all excited that
I finally managed to pull away from her!

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:34.960
You're easy to read.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.580
You wanna mess? Try saying that again.

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:39.960
You pilot with perfect spatial awareness.
It's a beautiful sight.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.090
Now you've got me feeling all conflicted...

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:45.080
It's that well-mannered sort of flying
that gets you shot down!

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:49.040
Chika, you'd actually do well to learn
to pilot a bit more carefully like she does.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:50.040
What?!

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.330
She's right, you know.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:54.830
Kylie probably flies the 
best out of all of us.

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:58.630
I'm sure it's all just instinct for her,
but she could easily be a flight instructor.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.380
It's one of the great mysteries of our squad!

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:02.460
You think so?

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:05.020
There's no element of surprise to her.

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:06.750
Nor a hint of self-control.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:08.000
Or a drop of composure.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:12.080
And by that they mean,
deal with those issues and you'll be unstoppable.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:16.880
I get the whole self-control and composure bit,
but "element of surprise?"

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:18.880
What the heck does that even mean?

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:19.710
Reona.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:22.290
Requesting permission of leave for tomorrow.

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:23.080
Tomorrow?

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:23.800
Yes.

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:25.470
Of course, you can go!

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:33.580
Where does Kate always go off to?

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:35.250
To go visit her brother in 
the hospital, apparently.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:37.790
She never came to visit me!

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:39.880
And neither did I.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:42.080
Reona and Zara did, though!

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:43.750
Did they now? Great. Lucky you.

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:46.830
But like, does she really 
have to go visit so often?

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:47.710
I guess so.

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:50.540
Is this part of that whole "species survival" thing
she was talking about?

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:51.200
Are you serious?

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.500
Reality is stranger than 
fiction, or so they say.

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:55.500
Have you ever even read 
a work of fiction, Chika?

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:58.130
I love books! My favorite is "See the Sea"!

00:05:58.130 --> 00:06:00.420
It's the first book my brother 
Chito ever read to me.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.380
Just the thought of that is ridiculous!

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:03.290
Oh, shut up!

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:07.290
When we lived down below, we had so many books,
and I read lots of them!

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:09.830
"See the Sea" all takes place under water.

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:12.380
There's not even a single scene on land.
But you knew that, right?

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:13.170
What?!

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:15.580
'Course, I did.

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:19.000
Mmm! This is splendid!

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.520
That rich taste and perfect sweetness.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.170
This is distilled liquor, isn't it?

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:26.000
The aged sort that the Yufang 
brought in, I'd wager.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.580
I'm surprised you even 
got your hands on this.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:29.700
I bought it off an antiques 
dealer in Areshima.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.170
For a fine price, I'm sure.

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:33.720
With no record of where 
it came from and no desire

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:37.030
to crack it open, it was 
simply taking up space.

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:38.310
It was quite inexpensive.

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:40.630
Well, I suppose when the 
bottle looks like that...

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:42.250
What are they doing?

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.330
It definitely doesn't look like 
any sort of "species survival".

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:45.460
I brought this as well.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:46.670
You really found it.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:48.330
Out in Areshima?

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:51.430
Is your research coming along?

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:54.710
Mhmm, but I still need more sources.

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:58.460
This would all be much easier
if I could still walk on my own.

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:01.210
Do you want to travel to Yufang, Allen?

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:03.130
Of course, I'd like to see it for myself.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:08.160
But more than, that I want to 
know why they showed up here

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:09.990
and then just vanished.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:11.630
Let me make one thing clear...

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:16.960
I'm not researching them simply because
I have a taste for Yufang alcohol!

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:18.540
I know.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:22.460
It looks like I was right to 
leave you in Reona's hands.

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:24.630
You smile a lot more than you used to.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:26.630
How's the KOTOBUKI Corps?

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:28.080
Having fun?

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:30.130
I'm not sure.

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:32.580
Have you ever seen Kate smile before?

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:35.830
Nope. And I've never seen her get mad
or cry or anything either.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:37.540
I'll come by again.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:39.680
Say hi to Reona for me.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:42.250
Tell her she should bring a nice bottle,
and come by and visit sometime.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:46.130
I guess he sorta looks like Kate...

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:48.460
But he's so talkative, and he drinks, too.

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:49.460
I do, yes.

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:52.000
Are you two in the KOTOBUKI Corps, too?

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:53.790
Uhh, well...

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:54.960
Y-yes.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.750
You probably have to look after Kate plenty.

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:59.130
How is she? Does she get along with everyone?

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:02.290
I mean, she's a total weirdo 
sometimes, but yeah.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:05.630
Hey, hey, how did you know we were out here?

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:08.460
Guess it's just my old 
pilot senses kicking in.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:11.750
Always need to stay aware 
of your surroundings, right?

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:15.380
I'm pretty sure Kate realized 
you were out here, too.

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:16.020
What...?

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:17.510
Yes. I did.

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:24.290
Allen told me he met Reona 
back when he was a pilot.

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:26.580
Yeah? What did he used to fly?

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:28.080
When is he gonna get better?

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:29.580
It's most likely he never will.

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:37.500
Huh? Kate?

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:41.920
Kate, what are you always reading about?

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:46.180
Mathematics, chemistry, thermodynamics,
fluid mechanics...

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:48.130
And as of late, electromagnetism.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:48.960
What about stories?

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.160
Or novels or something?

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.960
Fiction is pointless.

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:54.750
The author is free to 
write whatever they wish.

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:56.670
There is nothing to gain from such.

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:58.500
You don't even find them fun?

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:00.080
"Fun?"

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:02.500
Stories are like food for the soul!

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:04.250
That's what my brother Chito used to say!

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:06.580
I'll lend you "See the Sea" sometime, 'kay?

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:07.790
It's a real treat!

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:19.440
What a dreary, awful smelling place.

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:21.330
I'm sick of these sort of joints.

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:24.380
But that's where its charm lies, is it not?

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:25.170
Huh?

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.670
That's a Standon Oil plane.

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:32.290
What are big shot capitalists like them
doing way the hell out here?

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:35.340
Any leads, pops?

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:37.670
'Course I don't got any leads!

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:41.080
What were you even thinking trying
to round up people out here?

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:42.710
No one showed up, then?

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:45.640
The towns likely to dry up faster 
than their oil at this rate.

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:49.790
You watch your mouth!
That oil's all that's keeping us afloat!

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:51.580
That one tiny little oil well?

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:53.950
It's good enough!

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:57.180
We've even got those Standon boys
coming out trying to buy it up!

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:58.990
So that's what they're doing way out here.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:01.380
Well, you guys strike up a deal yet?

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:02.380
Like hell we did!

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:05.670
They showed up here ready 
to buy us straight out!

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:06.920
Sounds like good news to me.

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:09.500
You try working under those guys, then!

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.990
They'll just push us for bigger numbers
until we drive ourselves under.

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:14.380
I tell you, it's not about quantity anymore,
it's about quality!

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:15.590
Is it, now?

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:18.580
I'm working up a new type of gasoline.

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:21.550
Showin' those youngins what for!

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:24.250
Not that anyone out here's 
really young anymore!

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:28.710
Sounds like you're still the boss
of things 'round here, pops.

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:29.750
You keep at it.

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:31.790
Oh, you bet your butts I will!

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:36.210
I'll be pumping those junk piles you fly
with 100 octane gas, you'll see!

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:44.280
It might be high time 
for me to close up shop.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.380
What would you even do without your Shiden?

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:49.080
Live a life of love. It's 
all about love, my friend.

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:50.500
You're the last one I wanna hear that from.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:51.790
No, I mean it.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:54.830
I'll head out someplace with lots of people,
find me a nice gal.

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:56.380
There's no such life for me.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:01.600
My hands are dyed red with blood.

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:03.350
You're not gonna try and repent?

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:07.480
Even if the father above were to absolve me,
I could never forgive myself.

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:10.750
See, that's the part of you 
I think you need to work on.

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:12.250
I wish I could.

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:16.040
What was that?! What's going on?!

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:20.330
What the heck is all this?!

00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:23.000
Pops, this is bad. You 
need to get outta here!

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.130
The hell, I will!

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:26.880
You think I'm gonna let a little 
fire like this scare me off?

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:29.750
Utsumi! Yamada! Go call for help!

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:31.920
I'm gonna need more than 
these old farts here!

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:32.750
On it!

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:36.960
We're done for if this baby blows.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:40.500
Shouldn't you be worried 
more about an evacuation?

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:42.040
And just let the little town burn?

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:44.140
We should take this.

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:47.080
Now Kate, mind explaining to me why?

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:49.960
If we were to lose our access to Nanko's gas,

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:52.180
we'd be forced to deal with other oil fields.

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:53.190
Ones further away and far more expensive.

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:56.400
That will leave us with no choice but
to purchase from

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.160
affordable places like Standon.

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:00.500
But Standon's gas is poor in quality.

00:12:00.830 --> 00:12:04.420
And they are likely to monopolize the industry
and spike up their prices.

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:08.690
Plus, without access to a source 
as geographically close as Nanko,

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:10.810
we may risk being blockaded entirely.

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:13.040
Worst case scenario, we remain 
grounded indefinitely.

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:16.050
Nanko doesn't have cash,

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:18.530
but they're offering to pay with 
one years worth of gasoline.

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:19.510
Well, that will hardly do.

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:21.750
That's the Madame for you. Heartless.

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:25.370
They'll need to offer us 
reduced rates indefinitely.

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:27.760
And guarantee we'll have 
access to the fuel we need.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:29.920
Or else our hands our tied.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.750
So be it. You have a deal.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:35.270
But we need you to stomp 
out every last flame.

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:36.830
But, of course.

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:39.960
Now, how many hands on the 
ground do we need for this?

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:41.210
We don't need any.

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:42.380
How are you going to put the fire out?

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:43.040
With an explosive.

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:45.040
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:52.830
Why do I have to fly the bomber?

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:54.500
What else are you going to fly?

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:56.380
Your plane got shot down, remember?

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:58.750
You're best suited for this.

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:01.130
You can make the best of any aircraft.

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:05.710
We're just barely within flying range.
We'll need to stick to the shortest route.

00:13:05.710 --> 00:13:08.040
Did we really even need to come
out in numbers like these?

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:09.350
Don't we just need to drop this bomb?

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:12.330
Madame's orders. Says somethings
just not right about all this.

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:13.580
Told us to be careful.

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:15.170
Pops...

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:21.960
Gosh, darn it! This heat's a scorcher!

00:13:23.630 --> 00:13:24.540
There it is!

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:26.790
I let 'em know we'll be bombing the fire out.

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:29.160
Told 'em to get to safety.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.390
The whole place is up in flames, huh...

00:13:31.390 --> 00:13:32.040
Hmm?

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:38.000
The Madame's never wrong, is she?

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.960
Looks like company's coming out to greet us.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:41.000
What are they flying?

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.580
Shokis, maybe?

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:44.820
It might be the same group 
that hit the airfield.

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:46.840
If they're flying Type 
2s, we can handle them.

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:51.350
Stay alert!

00:13:57.880 --> 00:13:59.460
Those aren't Type 2s, they're Type 4s!

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:01.540
They're flying Hayates?

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:02.880
What kinda air pirates have Hayates?!

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:04.460
They're built basically 
the same as the Type 2s.

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:06.790
Just with more power and better turning!

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:11.030
Why do stinking air pirates 
get to fly such fast planes?

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:12.040
That's not fair!

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:13.710
Are these really even pirates?

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:17.170
Oh, come on, why do we have to deal with
this sort of stuff on today of all days?

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:18.500
I can't even fight back!

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:20.540
Leave 'em to me!

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:21.420
Hey, wait!

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:26.630
Gah, come on!

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:39.080
Bwah! Kate, we're gonna dodge 'em!

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:39.710
Roger.

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:56.210
I can't shoot if they get below us.

00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:57.920
Gah, I wish we could make a roll!

00:14:57.920 --> 00:14:58.460
Absolutely not.

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:01.170
They're so fast!

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:02.960
Chika, I'll act as bait!

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:03.790
Roger that!

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:18.690
Got-

00:15:18.690 --> 00:15:19.790
-none?!

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:21.670
The Type 4 has is heavily armored.

00:15:21.670 --> 00:15:22.830
Aim for its weak points!

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:23.960
What weak points?!

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:25.330
The tail!

00:15:32.250 --> 00:15:34.620
C'mon!

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:35.500
Dangit!

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:36.210
Above you!

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:39.170
Dammit!

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:40.330
Adolfo!

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:42.880
Damn, these guys are pros!

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:49.970
Chika?!

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:51.090
Now you're mine!

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:00.210
Gotcha!

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:05.170
Gah! You're a stubborn one, aren't ya!

00:16:05.170 --> 00:16:06.330
Chika! On your tail!

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:07.330
Grrr!

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:12.330
They're mine now.

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:13.370
Emma, above you!

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:15.750
What is it with these horrid pests?!

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:18.170
Were in a bad spot up against these guys.

00:16:18.170 --> 00:16:19.710
They aren't playing around.

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:23.000
Oh my!

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:23.540
Zara!

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:32.460
Zara, do you copy?!

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:35.140
Well, this is just wonderful...

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:45.290
Pops...

00:16:46.330 --> 00:16:47.910
Ah, dangit!

00:16:47.910 --> 00:16:51.630
If I gotta die, I wish it was at least
together with some nice lass.

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:57.990
Kylie, if things look bad, drop that bomb
and make an emergency landing!

00:16:57.990 --> 00:16:59.720
No way! We're putting out those fires!

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:03.330
Kylie, approach our target from our eight o'clock.
Then veer off at two o'clock.

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:04.040
Okay!

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:12.500
Kylie, 30 degrees to your right.

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:13.130
Got it!

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:21.580
Pull up to two thousand.

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:22.960
Here we go!

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:28.310
Kylie, roll us one eighty degrees.

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:29.480
What? R-right?

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:33.290
Perfect.

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:44.000
Damn!

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:45.500
They're toast at this rate!

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:48.540
Adolfo, there's something I wanted
to apologize to you for.

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:53.220
That Yufang liquor you had hidden away?
I'm the one who drank it.

00:17:53.220 --> 00:17:54.290
I hope you can forgive me.

00:17:54.290 --> 00:17:56.500
Hey, where's this coming 
from, all of a sudden?

00:17:56.970 --> 00:17:57.790
Wait!

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:17.920
Fernando! I forgive you! 
I forgive you, okay?!

00:18:17.920 --> 00:18:19.370
Just don't go doing anything stupid!

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:31.210
Fernando!

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:37.040
Damn you... You and your 
battlefield confessional!

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:39.040
I take that back, I don't forgive you!

00:18:46.170 --> 00:18:47.540
Kate, what are you doing?!

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:48.420
Lighting the fuse.

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:49.460
This is an IED, after all.

00:18:50.420 --> 00:18:51.480
I've already calculated the timing.

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:53.750
Kylie, drop the load when 
we're 200 meters out.

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:55.130
You sure we can't drop it a little earlier?

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:55.750
Absolutely not.

00:18:55.750 --> 00:18:57.540
I can feel my butt puckering already!

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:00.830
800 meters.

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:04.250
600 meters.

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:06.290
Ready...

00:19:07.670 --> 00:19:08.080
Go.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:08.790
Hiyah!

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:20.790
Kylie, good work.

00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:24.720
Fires extinguished.

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:31.420
Now's a convenient time to take off...

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:32.920
Who were those guys?

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:37.880
Looks like the winds of fortune 
fell upon us after all!

00:19:43.380 --> 00:19:46.920
I'm telling ya, this place still reeks.

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:49.380
And that's what it feels like to be alive!

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:53.580
Nothing but a cold beer tastes 
quite like life itself!

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:54.080
Yes...

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:57.080
I sure didn't feel alive out there today.

00:19:57.080 --> 00:19:59.130
I don't wanna fly anything 
but a fighter plane again.

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:01.750
I didn't even score a single tag today!

00:20:02.170 --> 00:20:03.470
At least you aren't down one like me.

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:06.130
Our mission was just to put out that fire.

00:20:06.130 --> 00:20:07.880
No need to go keeping score.

00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:10.150
And we pulled it off!

00:20:10.150 --> 00:20:11.750
That's one more win for us!

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:13.500
Who the heck were those guys, anyway?

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:16.040
Were they trying to dispose 
of the oil field in Nanko?

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:18.750
If this was the first time
they ever showed up, that might explain it.

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:20.000
But there's been so much more.

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:21.250
Yeah...

00:20:21.250 --> 00:20:24.710
Nanko seems like it'll dry up sooner or
later on its own, anyway.

00:20:24.710 --> 00:20:26.880
All we can say is, they 
sure aren't air pirates.

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:28.290
We're dealing with a well-led organization.

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:31.080
Led to do the absolute worst of deeds, is it?

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:32.710
That's what seems off about it all.

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:35.960
It says here, "The sea is whispering..."

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:37.920
But the sea is not a living being.

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:40.170
It doesn't mean it literally 
was, it's just a metaphor!

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:42.250
Stories like these don't just 
explain everything like that.

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:46.380
You're supposed to build the world
for yourself as you read it!

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:47.170
Build it...?

00:20:47.170 --> 00:20:48.710
That's what my brother Chito always said!

00:20:48.710 --> 00:20:49.830
Is that "See the Sea?"

00:20:50.420 --> 00:20:53.210
Wasn't there some drunkard 
just like Allen in that story?

00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:56.830
A person who loved his drink so much he tried
to keep all the liquor to himself.

00:20:56.830 --> 00:20:58.420
Well, more of a crab than a person.

00:20:58.420 --> 00:20:59.420
All to himself...?

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:02.790
Down under the sea there were
these springs of alcohol, see?

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:07.630
And this one crab who lived by one just
wanted to drink even more and more.

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:10.710
Oh my, sounds like the 
drink is what drunk him!

00:21:10.710 --> 00:21:13.040
And so he thought up a plan.

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:19.340
If he plugged up all the other springs,
he figured more would shoot up from his.

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:21.750
Speaking of things that seem off...

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:27.420
Well, in the end, he just ends up running his
own spring dry, and no longer gets to drink.

00:21:27.420 --> 00:21:30.430
I bet those black Hayates just wanna keep
all the liquor to themselves, too!

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.840
You think they're traveling the 
world, plugging up wherever

00:21:32.840 --> 00:21:34.840
it comes from so they can control it all?

00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:36.920
That'd be some grand sort of plan.

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:38.670
Hey, I think Kate's smiling!

00:21:38.670 --> 00:21:39.460
No way!

00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:42.540
Uh, yeah.

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:44.830
I'm totally not seeing it.

00:21:45.330 --> 00:21:47.370
It's just as I reported.

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:51.140
Those KOTOBUKI girls hit us once again.

00:21:51.140 --> 00:21:52.210
Very well.

00:21:53.670 --> 00:21:55.250
As you wish.

00:22:04.510 --> 00:22:08.630
I wanted to try and soar through that sky

00:22:08.630 --> 00:22:12.430
So I wished upon the winds right before me

00:22:12.430 --> 00:22:16.380
Our aspirations build us scenery

00:22:16.380 --> 00:22:20.790
I wonder how that wind is now

00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:29.130
Why do we fight, I wonder

00:22:29.130 --> 00:22:33.170
What is our purpose here?

00:22:33.170 --> 00:22:41.420
I asked, but the skies do not answer

00:22:42.090 --> 00:22:49.080
We all have wings

00:22:49.080 --> 00:22:53.790
Far away at the end of all lament

00:22:53.790 --> 00:22:58.180
The stories we found

00:22:58.180 --> 00:23:05.780
No one can steal these skies away

00:23:05.780 --> 00:23:10.500
We will soar unafraid of anything

00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:17.670
Because happiness is right here

00:23:26.010 --> 00:23:27.510
Preview

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:37.670
Next time on The Magnificent KOTOBUKI,
"The Great Airship Robbery"!

00:23:38.290 --> 00:23:41.040
The Great Airship Robbery
